window.COURSE_L1 = {"title": "Level - 1 Training Prework", "lessons": [{"index": 0, "title": "What is Think and Make?", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch this video to understand Think & Make[[/H]]"}, {"type": "video", "key": "CM1_Video 1_T&M Intro SL_D1_With Subtitles.mp4", "duration": 192}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Let's hear about Think & Make and what being an SL means from old student leaders and students", "audio": "8ef19d31-47ca-4207-af25-6d749f10d38b.mp3"}, {"type": "video", "key": "SL-Andole.mp4", "duration": 52}, {"type": "video", "key": "School Students 1.mp4", "duration": 164}, {"type": "video", "key": "6th kowkoor 2.mp4", "duration": 30}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Choose the correct option[[/H]]\nAnswer the question based on the video and your own understanding."}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Think & Make helps students learn by doing.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Think & Make program is only about finding the correct answer to a problem.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": false}, {"text": "False", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Students work in teams during Think & Make.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Future jobs may need skills like teamwork and creativity.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "How long is one Think & Make session?", "options": [{"text": "45 min", "correct": false}, {"text": "90 min", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Doing the right thing, even when no one is watching, defines true leadership."}]}, {"index": 1, "title": "Student Leader's Journey", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Being Student Leader can be scary, watch this video to see what skills you are developing by being an essential part of the Think and Make program[[/H]]\nWatch the video to learn about student leader's journey!", "audio": "cbf6f261-0898-408c-9518-208da11f862e.mp3"}, {"type": "video", "key": "Common Module 2_RC.mp4", "duration": 350}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise Time: Choose the correct answers for the questions below[[/H]]\n[[B]]Choose the correct option to learn more problem solving skills[[/B]]", "audio": "56b12592-93e8-4d03-8b2b-fc825fe7233e.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "One student looks disappointed because their team's idea was not chosen.", "options": [{"text": "Ignore them and continue.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Say, \"Your idea has many good points, lets discuss your idea?\"", "correct": true}, {"text": "Ask another student to talk to them.", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "The paper cups needed for today's activity are not available.", "options": [{"text": "Cancel the activity.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Wait until someone brings them.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask the teams, \"What else can we use instead?\"", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Your team finalized the first idea they thought of to solve the problem", "options": [{"text": "Tell them to use that idea to save time.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask, \"Can we think of two more ideas before we choose one?", "correct": true}, {"text": "Give them your own idea", "correct": false}]}]}, {"index": 2, "title": "Student Leader's Toolkit", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Student Leaders have three important tools for successfully completing the program in their clusters.[[/H]]\nStudent Leaders have three important tools to help them in the program"}, {"type": "list", "items": ["Team Workbook", "MiniMakers Space", "People around You"]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Lets take a look at the team workbook.[[/H]]"}, {"type": "video", "key": "Common Module 3_With Subtitles_D4.mp4", "duration": 388}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Lets look at some actions you need to do during the program . Press the play icon to listen to the list.[[/H]]"}, {"type": "steps", "steps": [{"title": "Before Session", "text": "• Read the session completely\n• Confirm session timing and pen drive location with teacher\n• Inform your cluster to be present on the day of the session\n• Practise saying the long instructions out loud in your own style\n• Think about the last session, and remember who needs extra help\n• If anything is not clear, ask your teacher for help", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T08_55_07_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}, {"title": "During Session", "text": "• Go through pages in order - explain activities in your own words in Telugu, not word to word from the book.\n• Use the Answer guide to help your cluster. Most activities have many correct answers, not just one.\n• Remind your cluster about time, 1 minute before time is up.\n• If a word from last session comes up, ask students what it means. If they have forgotten, explain it briefly.\n• After each activity, tell teams what they did well. Use questions to help them improve - not corrections.\n• Stay calm and patient. If a fight is too big to handle, ask the teacher - do not ignore it", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T09_24_36_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}, {"title": "After Session", "text": "• Put every material and the workbook back in Minimakers space and make sure it is locked\n• Discuss with fellow SLs about the session and any problem you had. They might help you solve it\n• If any student was causing trouble, inform the teacher.\n• If you have any doubts, note them down somewhere in the workbook, you can ask the IIF team in your next training.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T09_28_15_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "Practise Time: Choose the correct answer"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "If you have a doubt during a session, what should you check first?", "options": [{"text": "Mini Makerspace", "correct": false}, {"text": "Team Workbook", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "You see a Student Leader Say icon. What should you do?", "options": [{"text": "Skip it", "correct": false}, {"text": "Read and explain it", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "The video could not be played for some reason. What should you do next?", "options": [{"text": "Ask teacher to explain", "correct": false}, {"text": "Skip the activity", "correct": false}, {"text": "Use the pages in the workbook that explain the video", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Before training, what is your homework?", "options": [{"text": "Do the activities at home", "correct": false}, {"text": "Read the team workbook and marks pages you have questions about", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "impact", "text": "The common module is complete. Congratulations!\nNow, continue to your level course for the next part of the course."}]}, {"index": 3, "title": "Design Element: Shape", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch this video[[/H]]\nPlay the video to understand about 2 important design elements : Shape and Colour"}, {"type": "video", "key": "G7V3_D4_With Subtitles.mp4", "duration": 350}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Why Do Products Have Their Shape?[[/H]]\nHave you ever wondered why a football is round or why a brick is rectangular?\nThe shape of everyday objects is chosen for a reason.\nImagine if a football was square. It would be difficult to kick and wouldn't roll properly.\nNow imagine if a brick was round. It would be very difficult to stack.\nఎప్పుడైనా ఫుట్‌బాల్ ఎందుకు గుండ్రంగా ఉంటుందో, లేదా ఇటుక ఎందుకు దీర్ఘచతురస్ర ఆకారంలో ఉంటుందో ఆలోచించారా?\nమన రోజువారీ వస్తువుల ఆకారాన్ని ఒక కారణంతోనే ఎంచుకుంటారు.\nఒకవేళ ఫుట్‌బాల్ చతురస్రంగా ఉంటే, దాన్ని తన్నడం కష్టమవుతుంది. అలాగే అది సరిగ్గా దొర్లదు.\nఅలాగే, ఒకవేళ ఇటుక గుండ్రంగా ఉంటే, వాటిని ఒకదానిపై ఒకటి పేర్చడం చాలా కష్టమవుతుంది.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_20_07_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "ai-generated-image.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Shapes and Their Everyday Uses[[/H]]\nReview each flashcard to learn about common shapes and where you see them in real life."}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Circle", "bimg": "rolling-image-of-round-soccerball,-wheels-and-coins-in-3-sections-add-this-text-in-bottom-When-somet.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Rectangle", "bimg": "bricks-and-books,-making-stacking-and-storage-easy-and-stable.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Cylinder", "bimg": "A-visual-of-a-bottle-with-this-text--Used-for-bottles-and-cans,-making-them-easy-to-hold-and-pour-fr.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Hexagon", "bimg": "An-image-of-honeycomb-withthis-text--Seen-in-honeycombs,-allowing-strong,-space-saving-structures.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Semicircle", "bimg": "An-image-of-a-speedbump-and-rocking-chair-in-2-frame-with-the-text--Used-in-speed-bumps-and-rocking-.jpg", "back": ""}]}, {"type": "image", "src": "ChatGPT Image Jul 7, 2026, 10_57_16 AM.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Focus Skill- Critical Thinking[[/H]]\nAs you learn about design, you will also practise an important problem-solving skill called [[B]]Critical Thinking[[/B]].\nCritical Thinking means looking closely at the objects around you.\nBy observing carefully and breaking objects into parts, you can understand why they are designed that way.\nThis skill helps you identify what works, what doesn't, and how to create better designs.\n[[B]]Design[[/B]] గురించి నేర్చుకుంటూ, మీరు [[B]]Critical Thinking[[/B]] అనే ముఖ్యమైన [[B]]Problem-Solving Skill[[/B]] ను కూడా అభ్యసిస్తారు.\n[[B]]Critical Thinking[[/B]] అంటే మన చుట్టూ ఉన్న వస్తువులను జాగ్రత్తగా గమనించడం.\nవస్తువులను భాగాలుగా విడదీసి పరిశీలించడం ద్వారా, వాటిని అలా ఎందుకు [[B]]Design[[/B]] చేశారో అర్థం చేసుకోవచ్చు.\nఈ నైపుణ్యం వల్ల ఏది బాగా పనిచేస్తుందో, ఏది పనిచేయదో తెలుసుకొని, ఇంకా మంచి [[B]]Designs[[/B]] చేయగలుగుతారు.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_26_27_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Observing Small Details", "back": "Pay attention to small details when seeing, hearing, or touching objects to understand their uniqueness and usefulness.\nచిన్న విషయాలను గమనించండి."}, {"front": "Breaking Objects into Parts", "back": "Identify an object's parts and their functions to understand its design and functionality.\nవిషయాలను భాగాలుగా విభజించి వాటి పనితీరును అర్థం చేసుకోండి."}, {"front": "Example: A Bottle", "back": "A bottle has a body, neck, and cap. Each part has a specific shape and function.\nదాని భాగాలను గుర్తించి వాటి లక్షణాలను చర్చించండి."}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Choose the correct shape[[/H]]\nMatch each object with its correct shape.\nప్రతి product ని సరైన ఆకారంతో మ్యాచ్ చేయండి."}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Brick", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": true}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Water Bottle", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": true}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Honeycomb Cell", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Coin", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": true}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Carrom Board", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Square", "correct": true}, {"text": "Triangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "audio": "a82d280d-580d-473a-975f-053cca238219.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Pencil", "options": [{"text": "It looks attractive", "correct": false}, {"text": "It is easier to grip and doesn’t roll away", "correct": true}, {"text": "It is cheaper to make", "correct": false}, {"text": "It holds more lead", "correct": false}], "audio": "c40161d3-73e8-4d1d-90b7-3fd8b075dba8.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Changing the [[B]]shape[[/B]] of an object can make it more useful and solve problems better.\nNext, you'll learn how [[B]]colour[[/B]] is also an important part of design.\nColour can make products easier to use, safer, and more effective.\nLet's see how [[B]]colour[[/B]] helps in design!\nఒక వస్తువు యొక్క [[B]]Shape[[/B]] ను మార్చడం వల్ల అది మరింత ఉపయోగకరంగా మారి, సమస్యలను బాగా పరిష్కరించగలదు.\nతర్వాత, [[B]]Colour[[/B]] కూడా Design లో ఎంత ముఖ్యమైన పాత్ర పోషిస్తుందో తెలుసుకుందాం.\n[[B]]Colour[[/B]] వల్ల వస్తువులు ఉపయోగించడానికి సులభంగా, మరింత సురక్షితంగా మరియు ప్రభావవంతంగా మారతాయి.\n[[B]]Design[[/B]] లో [[B]]Colour[[/B]] ఎలా ఉపయోగపడుతుందో చూద్దాం!", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_33_38_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}]}, {"index": 4, "title": "Design Element: Colour", "blocks": [{"type": "impact", "text": "🔊 Listen", "audio": "Lesson_6_of_8_before_how_colour.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "image.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]The Power of Colour in Everyday Life[[/H]]\nHave you ever wondered why some objects are made in certain colours?\nLet's find out how [[B]]colour[[/B]] helps in design!\nకొన్ని వస్తువులు ప్రత్యేకమైన రంగుల్లోనే ఎందుకు ఉంటాయో ఎప్పుడైనా ఆలోచించారా?\n[[B]]Design[[/B]] లో [[B]]Colour[[/B]] ఎలా ఉపయోగపడుతుందో తెలుసుకుందాం"}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Primary and Secondary Colours in Design[[/H]]\nClick the boxes below to flip them, and then click on audio sign to know about that colour.", "audio": "371a8e38-376f-429b-97f8-3c4b63a13e75.mp3"}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Red", "fimg": "image.png", "audio": "cfc4dd9a-ee5a-490a-83d4-466d573b5ebf.mp3", "bimg": "A-primary-colour-often-used-for-stop-signs-and-emergency-signals-because-it-grabs-attention-quickly.jpg"}, {"front": "Blue", "fimg": "image-4.png", "audio": "97cc61a1-5dff-4d64-bb65-475c9ecaf9a0.mp3", "bimg": "A-picture-of-ink-pot-and-solar-panel.jpg"}, {"front": "Yellow", "fimg": "image-1.png", "audio": "f2ef6f9a-32d8-4ac6-8cba-c7f97ffe9638.mp3", "bimg": "A-primary-colour-chosen-for-school-buses-and-warning-signs-because-it-is-highly-visible,-even-in-low.jpg"}, {"front": "Orange", "fimg": "image-2.png", "audio": "256e89dd-b052-4199-a52b-570c1c5ab49c.mp3", "bimg": "A-traffic-cone-and-saftey-vest-in-orage-colour.jpg"}, {"front": "White / Light Blue", "fimg": "image-3.png", "audio": "dc5a9f05-6673-4d84-9820-e36338a845cd.mp3", "bimg": "An-open-fridge-and-a-white-doctors-coat.jpg"}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Why is a school bus usually painted yellow?\nస్కూల్ బస్ yellow కలర్ లోనే ఎందుకు ఉంటుంది?", "options": [{"text": "Yellow is a traditional colour", "correct": false}, {"text": "Yellow is easy to clean", "correct": false}, {"text": "Yellow is highly visible, even in low light", "correct": true}, {"text": "Yellow is the cheapest paint", "correct": false}], "audio": "906e11de-48b3-42ab-a24f-26c28a8800f1.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Colour as a Symbol[[/H]]\nColour is not just for looks.\nIt can also give us important information without using words.\nDesigners use colours to help people understand what to do.\nLet's see how [[B]]colour[[/B]] sends messages in our everyday lives!\n[[B]]Colour[[/B]] కేవలం అందంగా కనిపించడానికి మాత్రమే కాదు.\nమాటలు లేకుండానే ముఖ్యమైన సమాచారాన్ని కూడా చెబుతుంది.\nమనుషులు ఏమి చేయాలో అర్థమయ్యేలా Designers రంగులను ఉపయోగిస్తారు.\nమన రోజువారీ జీవితంలో [[B]]Colour[[/B]] ఎలా సందేశాలను ఇస్తుందో చూద్దాం!", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_48_06_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "ChatGPT Image Jul 6, 2026, 05_44_21 PM.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Choose the correct colour category of the Objects[[/H]]\nThink about [[B]]visibility[[/B]], [[B]]safety[[/B]], and [[B]]what the colour tells us[[/B]] before you choose.\nప్రతి వస్తువుకు సరిపోయే [[B]]Colour category[[/B]] తో జత చేయండి. ఎంచుకునే ముందు [[B]]సులభంగా కనిపించడం[[/B]], [[B]]భద్రత[[/B]], మరియు [[B]]ఆ రంగు చెప్పే అర్థం[[/B]] గురించి ఆలోచించండి."}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "School bus", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Emergency exit sign", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Wet waste bin", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": false}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Taxi number plate", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": false}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Red Firetruck", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Dry waste bin", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": false}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Black board", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Which colour would be best for a hospital sign and why?\nహాస్పిటల్ సైన్ కి సరిపోయే కలర్ ఏది? ఎందుకు?", "options": [{"text": "Red, because it signals danger", "correct": false}, {"text": "Green, because it means go", "correct": false}, {"text": "Blue, because it is calming and easy to read", "correct": true}, {"text": "Yellow, because it is bright", "correct": false}], "audio": "ea33c2d9-97dd-4270-a952-b43b42e71acf.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Congratulations! Now you understand 2 design elements - SHAPE & COLOUR. You are ready to guide your clusters!"}]}, {"index": 5, "title": "What is Biomimicry?", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch the Video[[/H]]\nPlay the video to understand about Biomimicry."}, {"type": "video", "key": "Biomimicry prework (1).mp4", "duration": null}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]What is Biomimicry?[[/H]]\nBiomimicry means getting ideas from nature to solve human problems or design better products.\nబయోమిమిక్రీ అంటే ప్రకృతిలోని ఆలోచనలను ఉపయోగించి మనుషుల సమస్యలకు పరిష్కారాలు కనుగొనడం లేదా మరింత మంచి products ను రూపొందించడం.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T18_15_02_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Breaking Down 'Biomimicry'[[/H]]\nLet’s get to know the word ‘biomimicry’!Click on each flashcard to break down the word and see what it really means."}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Bio", "back": "Bio means life or living things."}, {"front": "Mimic", "back": "Mimic means to copy or imitate something."}, {"front": "Biomimicry", "back": "Biomimicry is copying things from nature to help humans solve problems."}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Which things were inspired by nature?[[/H]]\nMatch each item with the correct category. Some are inventions inspired by nature, while others are just natural things or not related at all. Think carefully before you match!\nప్రతి వస్తువును సరైన categoryలో ఉంచండి. ఏవి ప్రకృతి నుంచి ప్రేరణ పొందిన ఆవిష్కరణలో (బయోమిమిక్రీ) భాగమో, ఏవి కాదో జాగ్రత్తగా ఆలోచించి వేరు చేయండి!"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Burdock Burr", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": true}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Plane", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": false}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Waterproof jacket", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": false}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Lotus leaf", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": true}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Bullet Train", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": false}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Bird", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": true}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "CCTV camera", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": false}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Kingfisher", "options": [{"text": "Nature", "correct": true}, {"text": "Inspired by Nature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "What is Biomimicry?\nబయోమిమిక్రీ అంటే?", "options": [{"text": "Use of ideas from nature to solve human problems", "correct": true}, {"text": "Copying the exact shape of plants and animals into products", "correct": false}, {"text": "Studying nature without using the ideas", "correct": false}, {"text": "Making products that look like animals", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "_________ is the first step of to design products using Biomimicry?\nబయోమిమిక్రీ వాడి products డిజైన్ చేయడానికి మొదటి స్టెప్ ఏంటి?", "options": [{"text": "Connect", "correct": false}, {"text": "Observe", "correct": true}, {"text": "Apply", "correct": false}, {"text": "Identify", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Nature’s ideas are everywhere! The next time you use something cool, ask: Could this be inspired by nature?"}]}, {"index": 6, "title": "How to use Biomimicry to design products?", "blocks": [{"type": "image", "src": "ai-generated-image-1.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "steps", "steps": [{"title": "Introduction: Become a Nature-Inspired Inventor", "text": "Get ready to become an inventor by following these simple steps inspired by nature.", "audio": null, "img": null}, {"title": "Summary: Turn Nature’s Ideas into Your Invention", "text": "By following these steps, you’ll turn a clever idea from nature into your very own invention!", "audio": null, "img": null}, {"title": "Observe", "text": "Look closely at a plant or animal and notice its special feature. What makes it stand out?", "audio": null, "img": null}, {"title": "Identify", "text": "Describe what makes this feature unique or helpful in nature. Why is it special?", "audio": null, "img": null}, {"title": "Connect", "text": "Think about how this feature could help solve a human problem. Where could it be useful?", "audio": null, "img": null}, {"title": "Apply", "text": "Imagine a product that uses this feature to help people.", "audio": null, "img": null}, {"title": "Sketch", "text": "Draw and label your product idea so others can understand it.", "audio": null, "img": null}]}, {"type": "image", "src": "ai-generated-image-2.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Which person is using biomimicry?\nకింద ఉన్న options లో ఎవరు Biomimicry వాడుతున్నారు?", "options": [{"text": "Ravi observes and paints a butterfly.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Meena observes a bird and makes a paper plane", "correct": true}, {"text": "Arun plants a tree and watches it grow everyday", "correct": false}, {"text": "Sita takes photographs of birds", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Which part of nature inspired Velcro?\nవెల్క్రో దేని నుంచి ప్రేరణ తీసుకొని తయారు చేసారు?", "options": [{"text": "A spider web", "correct": false}, {"text": "A plant burr with tiny hooks", "correct": true}, {"text": "A lizard's foot", "correct": false}, {"text": "A lotus leaf", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Congratulations! You've completed the pre-work. All the best for the Training![[/H]]"}]}]};
window.COURSE_L2 = {"title": "Level- 2 Training Prework", "lessons": [{"index": 0, "title": "What is Think and Make?", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch this video to understand Think & Make[[/H]]"}, {"type": "video", "key": "CM1_Video 1_T&M Intro SL_D1_With Subtitles.mp4", "duration": 192}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Let's hear about Think & Make and what being an SL means from old student leaders and students", "audio": "8ef19d31-47ca-4207-af25-6d749f10d38b.mp3"}, {"type": "video", "key": "SL-Andole.mp4", "duration": 52}, {"type": "video", "key": "School Students 1.mp4", "duration": 164}, {"type": "video", "key": "6th kowkoor 2.mp4", "duration": 30}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Choose the correct option[[/H]]\nAnswer the question based on the video and your own understanding."}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Think & Make helps students learn by doing.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Think & Make program is only about finding the correct answer to a problem.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": false}, {"text": "False", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Students work in teams during Think & Make.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Future jobs may need skills like teamwork and creativity.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "How long is one Think & Make session?", "options": [{"text": "45 min", "correct": false}, {"text": "90 min", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Doing the right thing, even when no one is watching, defines true leadership."}]}, {"index": 1, "title": "Student Leader's Journey", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Being Student Leader can be scary, watch this video to see what skills you are developing by being an essential part of the Think and Make program[[/H]]\nWatch the video to learn about student leader's journey!", "audio": "cbf6f261-0898-408c-9518-208da11f862e.mp3"}, {"type": "video", "key": "Common Module 2_RC.mp4", "duration": 350}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise Time: Choose the correct answers for the questions below[[/H]]\n[[B]]Choose the correct option to learn more problem solving skills[[/B]]", "audio": "56b12592-93e8-4d03-8b2b-fc825fe7233e.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "One student looks disappointed because their team's idea was not chosen.", "options": [{"text": "Ignore them and continue.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Say, \"Your idea has many good points, lets discuss your idea?\"", "correct": true}, {"text": "Ask another student to talk to them.", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "The paper cups needed for today's activity are not available.", "options": [{"text": "Cancel the activity.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Wait until someone brings them.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask the teams, \"What else can we use instead?\"", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Your team finalized the first idea they thought of to solve the problem", "options": [{"text": "Tell them to use that idea to save time.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask, \"Can we think of two more ideas before we choose one?", "correct": true}, {"text": "Give them your own idea", "correct": false}]}]}, {"index": 2, "title": "Student Leader's Toolkit", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Student Leaders have three important tools for successfully completing the program in their clusters.[[/H]]\nStudent Leaders have three important tools to help them in the program"}, {"type": "list", "items": ["Team Workbook", "MiniMakers Space", "People around You"]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Lets take a look at the team workbook.[[/H]]"}, {"type": "video", "key": "Common Module 3_With Subtitles_D4.mp4", "duration": 388}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Lets look at some actions you need to do during the program . Press the play icon to listen to the list.[[/H]]"}, {"type": "steps", "steps": [{"title": "Before Session", "text": "• Read the session completely\n• Confirm session timing and pen drive location with teacher\n• Inform your cluster to be present on the day of the session\n• Practise saying the long instructions out loud in your own style\n• Think about the last session, and remember who needs extra help\n• If anything is not clear, ask your teacher for help", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T08_55_07_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}, {"title": "During Session", "text": "• Go through pages in order - explain activities in your own words in Telugu, not word to word from the book.\n• Use the Answer guide to help your cluster. Most activities have many correct answers, not just one.\n• Remind your cluster about time, 1 minute before time is up.\n• If a word from last session comes up, ask students what it means. If they have forgotten, explain it briefly.\n• After each activity, tell teams what they did well. Use questions to help them improve - not corrections.\n• Stay calm and patient. If a fight is too big to handle, ask the teacher - do not ignore it", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T09_24_36_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}, {"title": "After Session", "text": "• Put every material and the workbook back in Minimakers space and make sure it is locked\n• Discuss with fellow SLs about the session and any problem you had. They might help you solve it\n• If any student was causing trouble, inform the teacher.\n• If you have any doubts, note them down somewhere in the workbook, you can ask the IIF team in your next training.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T09_28_15_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "Practise Time: Choose the correct answer"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "If you have a doubt during a session, what should you check first?", "options": [{"text": "Mini Makerspace", "correct": false}, {"text": "Team Workbook", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "You see a Student Leader Say icon. What should you do?", "options": [{"text": "Skip it", "correct": false}, {"text": "Read and explain it", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "The video could not be played for some reason. What should you do next?", "options": [{"text": "Ask teacher to explain", "correct": false}, {"text": "Skip the activity", "correct": false}, {"text": "Use the pages in the workbook that explain the video", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Before training, what is your homework?", "options": [{"text": "Do the activities at home", "correct": false}, {"text": "Read the team workbook and marks pages you have questions about", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "impact", "text": "The common module is complete. Congratulations!\nNow, continue to your level course for the next part of the course."}]}, {"index": 3, "title": "Understanding Users and User needs", "blocks": [{"type": "impact", "text": "🔊 Listen", "audio": "Lesson_4_of_8_intro_voice_over.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "users-computer-toddler-wheelchair.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "In product design, a [[B]]user[[/B]] is the person who uses a product. For example, if you use a bag to school, you are the user of that bag.\nA [[B]]user need[[/B]] is what the user wants the product to do for them. For example, you might need your backpack to be comfortable and big enough to carry your books. Designers think about these needs to make products that work well for different people.\n[[B]]User[[/B]] అంటే ఒక వస్తువును ఉపయోగించే వ్యక్తి. ఉదాహరణకు, మీరు [[B]]School Bag[[/B]] ఉపయోగిస్తే, [[B]]మీరు ఆ Bag కు User[[/B]]. [[B]]User Need[[/B]] అంటే, ఆ వస్తువు ఏమి చేయాలని [[B]]User[[/B]] కోరుకుంటాడో అది. ఉదాహరణకు, మీ [[B]]School Bag[[/B]] [[B]]సౌకర్యంగా ఉండాలి[[/B]] మరియు [[B]]మీ పుస్తకాలు అన్నీ పట్టాలి[[/B]]. మంచి [[B]]Designers[[/B]], ఏదైనా వస్తువును [[B]]Design[[/B]] చేసే ముందు [[B]]User Needs[[/B]] ను అర్థం చేసుకుంటారు.", "audio": null}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Why is the same product different for different people?[[/H]]\nLet's watch this video to understand about user, user needs and different products."}, {"type": "video", "key": "Grade 7_Video 2_with subtitles.mp4", "duration": 358}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Understanding User & User Needs[[/H]]\nClick on the flip sign to understand about user and product. Click on the audio sign to listen to the need of the user."}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Surgeon", "fimg": "Surgeon-image-with-surgeon-text-written-on-it.jpg", "back": "Needs to keep hands clean and safe—wears sterile gloves during surgery.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T10_06_44_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "bimg": "Surgery-gloves.jpg"}, {"front": "Welder", "fimg": "Welder-image-and-welder-written-on-it.jpg", "back": "Needs protection from heat and sparks—uses thick, heat-resistant gloves.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T10_09_37_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "bimg": "Welding-gloves.jpg"}, {"front": "Goalkeeper", "fimg": "Goal-keeper-image-and-goalkeeper-written-on-it.jpg", "back": "Needs a strong, padded grip to catch fast balls—wears cushioned goalkeeper gloves.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T10_12_03_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "bimg": "goalkeeper-gloves.jpg"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practice time: Choose the correct answer[[/H]]"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Which glove is best for a welder?", "options": [{"text": "Thin cotton gloves", "correct": false}, {"text": "Thick, heat-resistant gloves", "correct": true}, {"text": "Plastic disposable gloves", "correct": false}, {"text": "Fingerless gloves", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Match Users, Needs, and Product Features[[/H]]\nMatch each user to their specific need and the best product feature. Select each item to the correct category: User, Need, or Product Feature.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T10_14_55_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "A blind person can’t tell if their glass is full. What feature could a cup have to help them?", "options": [{"text": "Make the cup very colorful", "correct": false}, {"text": "Add a handle to the cup", "correct": false}, {"text": "Add a sound or vibration when the cup is full", "correct": true}, {"text": "Make the cup bigger", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Is it a Product, Need, or Feature?[[/H]]"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Sanitation worker\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": true}, {"text": "Need", "correct": false}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Needs protection from dirty water\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": false}, {"text": "Need", "correct": true}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Cushioned gloves\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": false}, {"text": "Need", "correct": false}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Shoes with good grip\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": false}, {"text": "Need", "correct": false}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Needs to stop fast balls\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": false}, {"text": "Need", "correct": true}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Elderly person\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": true}, {"text": "Need", "correct": false}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Goalkeeper\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": true}, {"text": "Need", "correct": false}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Needs comfortable, safe walking\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": false}, {"text": "Need", "correct": true}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Waterproof boots\nSelect category?", "options": [{"text": "User", "correct": false}, {"text": "Need", "correct": false}, {"text": "Product Feature", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "text", "text": "Understanding users and their needs is the secret to designing products that really help people. When you pay attention to who will use something and what they need, you can create solutions that make life easier and better."}]}, {"index": 4, "title": "Design Element: Shape", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch this video[[/H]]\nPlay the video to understand about 2 important design elements : Shape and Colour"}, {"type": "video", "key": "G7V3_D4_With Subtitles.mp4", "duration": 350}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Why Do Products Have Their Shape?[[/H]]\nHave you ever wondered why a football is round or why a brick is rectangular?\nThe shape of everyday objects is chosen for a reason.\nImagine if a football was square. It would be difficult to kick and wouldn't roll properly.\nNow imagine if a brick was round. It would be very difficult to stack.\nఎప్పుడైనా ఫుట్‌బాల్ ఎందుకు గుండ్రంగా ఉంటుందో, లేదా ఇటుక ఎందుకు దీర్ఘచతురస్ర ఆకారంలో ఉంటుందో ఆలోచించారా?\nమన రోజువారీ వస్తువుల ఆకారాన్ని ఒక కారణంతోనే ఎంచుకుంటారు.\nఒకవేళ ఫుట్‌బాల్ చతురస్రంగా ఉంటే, దాన్ని తన్నడం కష్టమవుతుంది. అలాగే అది సరిగ్గా దొర్లదు.\nఅలాగే, ఒకవేళ ఇటుక గుండ్రంగా ఉంటే, వాటిని ఒకదానిపై ఒకటి పేర్చడం చాలా కష్టమవుతుంది.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_20_07_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "ai-generated-image.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Shapes and Their Everyday Uses[[/H]]\nReview each flashcard to learn about common shapes and where you see them in real life."}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Circle", "bimg": "rolling-image-of-round-soccerball,-wheels-and-coins-in-3-sections-add-this-text-in-bottom-When-somet.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Rectangle", "bimg": "bricks-and-books,-making-stacking-and-storage-easy-and-stable.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Cylinder", "bimg": "A-visual-of-a-bottle-with-this-text--Used-for-bottles-and-cans,-making-them-easy-to-hold-and-pour-fr.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Hexagon", "bimg": "An-image-of-honeycomb-withthis-text--Seen-in-honeycombs,-allowing-strong,-space-saving-structures.jpg", "back": ""}, {"front": "Semicircle", "bimg": "An-image-of-a-speedbump-and-rocking-chair-in-2-frame-with-the-text--Used-in-speed-bumps-and-rocking-.jpg", "back": ""}]}, {"type": "image", "src": "ChatGPT Image Jul 7, 2026, 10_57_16 AM.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Focus Skill- Critical Thinking[[/H]]\nAs you learn about design, you will also practise an important problem-solving skill called [[B]]Critical Thinking[[/B]].\nCritical Thinking means looking closely at the objects around you.\nBy observing carefully and breaking objects into parts, you can understand why they are designed that way.\nThis skill helps you identify what works, what doesn't, and how to create better designs.\n[[B]]Design[[/B]] గురించి నేర్చుకుంటూ, మీరు [[B]]Critical Thinking[[/B]] అనే ముఖ్యమైన [[B]]Problem-Solving Skill[[/B]] ను కూడా అభ్యసిస్తారు.\n[[B]]Critical Thinking[[/B]] అంటే మన చుట్టూ ఉన్న వస్తువులను జాగ్రత్తగా గమనించడం.\nవస్తువులను భాగాలుగా విడదీసి పరిశీలించడం ద్వారా, వాటిని అలా ఎందుకు [[B]]Design[[/B]] చేశారో అర్థం చేసుకోవచ్చు.\nఈ నైపుణ్యం వల్ల ఏది బాగా పనిచేస్తుందో, ఏది పనిచేయదో తెలుసుకొని, ఇంకా మంచి [[B]]Designs[[/B]] చేయగలుగుతారు.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_26_27_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Observing Small Details", "back": "Pay attention to small details when seeing, hearing, or touching objects to understand their uniqueness and usefulness.\nచిన్న విషయాలను గమనించండి."}, {"front": "Breaking Objects into Parts", "back": "Identify an object's parts and their functions to understand its design and functionality.\nవిషయాలను భాగాలుగా విభజించి వాటి పనితీరును అర్థం చేసుకోండి."}, {"front": "Example: A Bottle", "back": "A bottle has a body, neck, and cap. Each part has a specific shape and function.\nదాని భాగాలను గుర్తించి వాటి లక్షణాలను చర్చించండి."}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Choose the correct shape[[/H]]\nMatch each object with its correct shape.\nప్రతి product ని సరైన ఆకారంతో మ్యాచ్ చేయండి."}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Brick", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": true}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Water Bottle", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": true}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Honeycomb Cell", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Coin", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": true}, {"text": "Rectangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Cylinder", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Carrom Board", "options": [{"text": "Circle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Square", "correct": true}, {"text": "Triangle", "correct": false}, {"text": "Hexagon", "correct": false}], "audio": "a82d280d-580d-473a-975f-053cca238219.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Pencil", "options": [{"text": "It looks attractive", "correct": false}, {"text": "It is easier to grip and doesn’t roll away", "correct": true}, {"text": "It is cheaper to make", "correct": false}, {"text": "It holds more lead", "correct": false}], "audio": "c40161d3-73e8-4d1d-90b7-3fd8b075dba8.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Changing the [[B]]shape[[/B]] of an object can make it more useful and solve problems better.\nNext, you'll learn how [[B]]colour[[/B]] is also an important part of design.\nColour can make products easier to use, safer, and more effective.\nLet's see how [[B]]colour[[/B]] helps in design!\nఒక వస్తువు యొక్క [[B]]Shape[[/B]] ను మార్చడం వల్ల అది మరింత ఉపయోగకరంగా మారి, సమస్యలను బాగా పరిష్కరించగలదు.\nతర్వాత, [[B]]Colour[[/B]] కూడా Design లో ఎంత ముఖ్యమైన పాత్ర పోషిస్తుందో తెలుసుకుందాం.\n[[B]]Colour[[/B]] వల్ల వస్తువులు ఉపయోగించడానికి సులభంగా, మరింత సురక్షితంగా మరియు ప్రభావవంతంగా మారతాయి.\n[[B]]Design[[/B]] లో [[B]]Colour[[/B]] ఎలా ఉపయోగపడుతుందో చూద్దాం!", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_33_38_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}]}, {"index": 5, "title": "Design Element: Colour", "blocks": [{"type": "impact", "text": "🔊 Listen", "audio": "Lesson_6_of_8_before_how_colour.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "image.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]The Power of Colour in Everyday Life[[/H]]\nHave you ever wondered why some objects are made in certain colours?\nLet's find out how [[B]]colour[[/B]] helps in design!\nకొన్ని వస్తువులు ప్రత్యేకమైన రంగుల్లోనే ఎందుకు ఉంటాయో ఎప్పుడైనా ఆలోచించారా?\n[[B]]Design[[/B]] లో [[B]]Colour[[/B]] ఎలా ఉపయోగపడుతుందో తెలుసుకుందాం"}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Primary and Secondary Colours in Design[[/H]]\nClick the boxes below to flip them, and then click on audio sign to know about that colour.", "audio": "371a8e38-376f-429b-97f8-3c4b63a13e75.mp3"}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Red", "fimg": "image.png", "audio": "cfc4dd9a-ee5a-490a-83d4-466d573b5ebf.mp3", "bimg": "A-primary-colour-often-used-for-stop-signs-and-emergency-signals-because-it-grabs-attention-quickly.jpg"}, {"front": "Blue", "fimg": "image-4.png", "audio": "97cc61a1-5dff-4d64-bb65-475c9ecaf9a0.mp3", "bimg": "A-picture-of-ink-pot-and-solar-panel.jpg"}, {"front": "Yellow", "fimg": "image-1.png", "audio": "f2ef6f9a-32d8-4ac6-8cba-c7f97ffe9638.mp3", "bimg": "A-primary-colour-chosen-for-school-buses-and-warning-signs-because-it-is-highly-visible,-even-in-low.jpg"}, {"front": "Orange", "fimg": "image-2.png", "audio": "256e89dd-b052-4199-a52b-570c1c5ab49c.mp3", "bimg": "A-traffic-cone-and-saftey-vest-in-orage-colour.jpg"}, {"front": "White / Light Blue", "fimg": "image-3.png", "audio": "dc5a9f05-6673-4d84-9820-e36338a845cd.mp3", "bimg": "An-open-fridge-and-a-white-doctors-coat.jpg"}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Why is a school bus usually painted yellow?\nస్కూల్ బస్ yellow కలర్ లోనే ఎందుకు ఉంటుంది?", "options": [{"text": "Yellow is a traditional colour", "correct": false}, {"text": "Yellow is easy to clean", "correct": false}, {"text": "Yellow is highly visible, even in low light", "correct": true}, {"text": "Yellow is the cheapest paint", "correct": false}], "audio": "906e11de-48b3-42ab-a24f-26c28a8800f1.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Colour as a Symbol[[/H]]\nColour is not just for looks.\nIt can also give us important information without using words.\nDesigners use colours to help people understand what to do.\nLet's see how [[B]]colour[[/B]] sends messages in our everyday lives!\n[[B]]Colour[[/B]] కేవలం అందంగా కనిపించడానికి మాత్రమే కాదు.\nమాటలు లేకుండానే ముఖ్యమైన సమాచారాన్ని కూడా చెబుతుంది.\nమనుషులు ఏమి చేయాలో అర్థమయ్యేలా Designers రంగులను ఉపయోగిస్తారు.\nమన రోజువారీ జీవితంలో [[B]]Colour[[/B]] ఎలా సందేశాలను ఇస్తుందో చూద్దాం!", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-06T17_48_06_Arabella - Mysterious and Emotive_pvc_sp100_s63_sb100_v3.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "ChatGPT Image Jul 6, 2026, 05_44_21 PM.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Choose the correct colour category of the Objects[[/H]]\nThink about [[B]]visibility[[/B]], [[B]]safety[[/B]], and [[B]]what the colour tells us[[/B]] before you choose.\nప్రతి వస్తువుకు సరిపోయే [[B]]Colour category[[/B]] తో జత చేయండి. ఎంచుకునే ముందు [[B]]సులభంగా కనిపించడం[[/B]], [[B]]భద్రత[[/B]], మరియు [[B]]ఆ రంగు చెప్పే అర్థం[[/B]] గురించి ఆలోచించండి."}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "School bus", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Emergency exit sign", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Wet waste bin", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": false}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Taxi number plate", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": false}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Red Firetruck", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Dry waste bin", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": false}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Black board", "options": [{"text": "Visibility and Safety", "correct": true}, {"text": "Symbolic Meaning", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Which colour would be best for a hospital sign and why?\nహాస్పిటల్ సైన్ కి సరిపోయే కలర్ ఏది? ఎందుకు?", "options": [{"text": "Red, because it signals danger", "correct": false}, {"text": "Green, because it means go", "correct": false}, {"text": "Blue, because it is calming and easy to read", "correct": true}, {"text": "Yellow, because it is bright", "correct": false}], "audio": "ea33c2d9-97dd-4270-a952-b43b42e71acf.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Let's understand the 3rd design element now."}]}, {"index": 6, "title": "Discovering Everyday Materials", "blocks": [{"type": "impact", "text": "🔊 Listen", "audio": "Lesson_7_of_8_intro_voice_over.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "materials-jar-bottle-woodblock.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]A [[B]]material[[/B]] is what an object is made of.[[/H]]For example, a chair can be made of [[B]]wood[[/B]], a bottle of [[B]]plastic[[/B]], and a window of [[B]]glass[[/B]].\nDifferent materials have different properties and uses.\nIn this lesson, you'll learn how to identify materials in everyday objects and understand why each material is chosen.\n[[B]]Material[[/B]] అంటే ఒక వస్తువు దేనితో తయారైందో అది.\nఉదాహరణకు, ఒక కుర్చీ [[B]]చెక్కతో[[/B]], ఒక బాటిల్ [[B]]ప్లాస్టిక్‌తో[[/B]], ఒక కిటికీ [[B]]గాజుతో[[/B]] తయారవుతుంది.\nప్రతి [[B]]Material[[/B]] కు వేర్వేరు లక్షణాలు మరియు ఉపయోగాలు ఉంటాయి.\nఈ పాఠంలో, రోజువారీ వస్తువులలో ఉన్న [[B]]Materials[[/B]] ను గుర్తించడం మరియు ప్రతి [[B]]Material[[/B]] ను ఎందుకు ఎంచుకున్నారో తెలుసుకుంటారు.", "audio": "1690a73e-2272-42e5-9853-33840085997a.mp3"}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Materials in Action: Where and Why[[/H]]\nLet's see how materials are used in real life.\nEvery object is made from a material for a reason.\n[[B]]Materials[[/B]] నిజ జీవితంలో ఎలా ఉపయోగపడతాయో చూద్దాం.\nప్రతి వస్తువును ఒక కారణంతోనే ఒక [[B]]Material[[/B]] తో తయారు చేస్తారు.\nవేర్వేరు ప్రదేశాల్లో, వేర్వేరు పనుల కోసం ఎందుకు వేర్వేరు [[B]]Materials[[/B]] ను ఎంచుకుంటారో తెలుసుకుందాం.", "audio": "454e27b7-b427-4be3-a8b6-2e1c18331f18.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "ChatGPT Image Jul 3, 2026, 03_46_56 PM.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[B]]Each number on the picture is one part of the house. Flip the matching card below to see which material it is made of, and why.[[/B]]\n[[B]]ఫోటోలోని ప్రతి నంబర్ ఇంటిలోని ఒక భాగం. ఆ భాగం ఏ Material తో తయారైందో, ఎందుకో తెలుసుకోవడానికి కింద ఉన్న కార్డును తిప్పండి.[[/B]]"}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "1\nMetal Gate", "back": "Strong, secure, allows airflow"}, {"front": "2\nWooden Door", "back": "Gives privacy and long lasting"}, {"front": "3\nGlass Window", "back": "Lets light in, feels open, transparent"}, {"front": "4\nPVC Door", "back": "Cheap and waterproof"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Common Everyday Materials Flashcards[[/H]]\nReview each flashcard to get familiar with some common materials you see every day. Try to guess the material before flipping the card to see the answer!"}, {"type": "flashcards", "cards": [{"front": "Wood", "back": "Wood is a hard, natural material from trees. It’s often used for furniture, doors, and pencils."}, {"front": "Plastic", "back": "Plastic is a lightweight, man-made material. It’s used for bottles, bags, toys, and many everyday items."}, {"front": "Metal", "back": "Metal is strong and shiny. You’ll find it in keys, coins, tools, and many machines."}, {"front": "Glass", "back": "Glass is clear and smooth. It’s used for windows, jars, and drinking glasses."}, {"front": "Fabric", "back": "Fabric is soft and flexible. Clothes, curtains, and bags are often made from different types of fabric."}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Properties of materials[[/H]]\nMaterials have some properties that make them useful for certain use, Let's read about the properties"}, {"type": "steps", "steps": [{"title": "Texture", "text": "Texture is how a material feels when touched.\nMaterial ని తాకినప్పుడు కలిగే అనుభూతినే(feel) texture అంటారు", "audio": null, "img": "G7 U1 Workbook.jpg"}, {"title": "Strength", "text": "Strength is how much force or weight something can handle without breaking.\nఒక వస్తువు ఎంత బరువును లేదా శక్తిని తట్టుకోగలదో అదే strength.", "audio": null, "img": "G7 U1 Workbook (1).jpg"}, {"title": "Flexibility", "text": "Flexibility is how easily a material bends without breaking.\nఒక material విరగకుండా సులభంగా వంగగలిగే గుణాన్నే flexibility అంటారు.", "audio": null, "img": "G7 U1 Workbook (3).jpg"}, {"title": "Water-resistance", "text": "Water-resistance is how materials do not absorb water easily.\nWater-resistant materials నీటిని సులభంగా పీల్చుకోవు.", "audio": null, "img": "G7 U1 Workbook (4).jpg"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Order the materials by strength[[/H]]\nChoose the correct strength for each material, from the least strong to the most strong.\n[[B]]ప్రతి Material కి సరైన బలాన్ని ఎంచుకోండి.[[/B]]"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Plastic", "options": [{"text": "Least strong", "correct": true}, {"text": "Moderately strong", "correct": false}, {"text": "Strongest", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Wood", "options": [{"text": "Least strong", "correct": false}, {"text": "Moderately strong", "correct": true}, {"text": "Strongest", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Metal", "options": [{"text": "Least strong", "correct": false}, {"text": "Moderately strong", "correct": false}, {"text": "Strongest", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise Time: Choose the correct materials for these objects[[/H]]\n[[B]]Let's test your skills![[/B]]\nThink carefully before you choose!\n[[B]]ఇప్పుడు మీ నైపుణ్యాలను పరీక్షించుకుందాం![[/B]]\nప్రతి వస్తువును అది సాధారణంగా తయారయ్యే [[B]]Material[[/B]] తో జత చేయండి.\nఎంచుకునే ముందు బాగా ఆలోచించండి!", "audio": "b013c9a3-5ded-4d2b-98c0-a1ec3c0150f0.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "School bag", "options": [{"text": "Metal", "correct": false}, {"text": "Plastic", "correct": false}, {"text": "Wood", "correct": false}, {"text": "Fabric", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Kitchen pan", "options": [{"text": "Metal", "correct": true}, {"text": "Plastic", "correct": false}, {"text": "Wood", "correct": false}, {"text": "Fabric", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Toy", "options": [{"text": "Metal", "correct": false}, {"text": "Plastic", "correct": true}, {"text": "Wood", "correct": false}, {"text": "Fabric", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Bat", "options": [{"text": "Metal", "correct": false}, {"text": "Plastic", "correct": false}, {"text": "Wood", "correct": true}, {"text": "Fabric", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}]}, {"index": 7, "title": "Practise Time: Material Properties", "blocks": [{"type": "image", "src": "ai-generated-image-3.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Raincoat Materials: Does It Matter?[[/H]]\nImagine two raincoats that look exactly the same.\nThey have the same [[B]]shape[[/B]] and [[B]]colour[[/B]].\nBut one is made of [[B]]plastic[[/B]] and the other is made of [[B]]wool[[/B]].\nWhich one will keep you dry in the rain?\nThe [[B]]material[[/B]] makes all the difference!\nఒకేలా కనిపించే రెండు [[B]]Raincoats[[/B]] ఉన్నాయని ఊహించండి.\nరెండింటికీ ఒకే [[B]]Shape[[/B]], ఒకే [[B]]Colour[[/B]] ఉంటుంది.\nకానీ ఒకటి [[B]]Plastic[[/B]] తో, మరొకటి [[B]]Wool[[/B]] తో తయారైంది.\nవర్షంలో ఏది మిమ్మల్ని పొడిగా ఉంచుతుంది?\n[[B]]Material[[/B]] వల్లే తేడా వస్తుంది!", "audio": "accf6d9c-8d20-4b6e-8218-42783eb11653.mp3"}, {"type": "image", "src": "ai-generated-image-4.jpg", "caption": ""}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Which material would you choose for a bathroom floor?", "options": [{"text": "Smooth tile", "correct": false}, {"text": "Rough tile", "correct": true}, {"text": "Wooden plank", "correct": false}, {"text": "Paper mat", "correct": false}], "audio": "7a63dde5-a4d6-4a84-bc8c-460f9a3f70d1.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "A doctor needs a tube for curved pathways", "options": [{"text": "Needs Strength", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Flexibility", "correct": true}, {"text": "Needs Water Resistance", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Texture/Grip", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "A hiker’s map gets wet in the rain", "options": [{"text": "Needs Strength", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Flexibility", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Water Resistance", "correct": true}, {"text": "Needs Texture/Grip", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "A plastic bat breaks quickly", "options": [{"text": "Needs Strength", "correct": true}, {"text": "Needs Flexibility", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Water Resistance", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Texture/Grip", "correct": false}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "A grandmother slips on smooth tiles", "options": [{"text": "Needs Strength", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Flexibility", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Water Resistance", "correct": false}, {"text": "Needs Texture/Grip", "correct": true}], "sortItem": true}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Smart designers always match the right material to the job. The right choice makes things safer, stronger, and longer-lasting!"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Congratulations! Now you understand 3 design elements. You are ready to guide your clusters!"}]}]};
window.COURSE_L3 = {"title": "Level- 3 Training Prework", "lessons": [{"index": 0, "title": "What is Think and Make?", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch this video to understand Think & Make[[/H]]"}, {"type": "video", "key": "CM1_Video 1_T&M Intro SL_D1_With Subtitles.mp4", "duration": 192}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Let's hear about Think & Make and what being an SL means from old student leaders and students", "audio": "8ef19d31-47ca-4207-af25-6d749f10d38b.mp3"}, {"type": "video", "key": "SL-Andole.mp4", "duration": 52}, {"type": "video", "key": "School Students 1.mp4", "duration": 164}, {"type": "video", "key": "6th kowkoor 2.mp4", "duration": 30}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise time: Choose the correct option[[/H]]\nAnswer the question based on the video and your own understanding."}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Think & Make helps students learn by doing.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Think & Make program is only about finding the correct answer to a problem.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": false}, {"text": "False", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Students work in teams during Think & Make.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Future jobs may need skills like teamwork and creativity.", "options": [{"text": "True", "correct": true}, {"text": "False", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "How long is one Think & Make session?", "options": [{"text": "45 min", "correct": false}, {"text": "90 min", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "impact", "text": "Doing the right thing, even when no one is watching, defines true leadership."}]}, {"index": 1, "title": "Student Leader's Journey", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Being Student Leader can be scary, watch this video to see what skills you are developing by being an essential part of the Think and Make program[[/H]]\nWatch the video to learn about student leader's journey!", "audio": "cbf6f261-0898-408c-9518-208da11f862e.mp3"}, {"type": "video", "key": "Common Module 2_RC.mp4", "duration": 350}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise Time: Choose the correct answers for the questions below[[/H]]\n[[B]]Choose the correct option to learn more problem solving skills[[/B]]", "audio": "56b12592-93e8-4d03-8b2b-fc825fe7233e.mp3"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "One student looks disappointed because their team's idea was not chosen.", "options": [{"text": "Ignore them and continue.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Say, \"Your idea has many good points, lets discuss your idea?\"", "correct": true}, {"text": "Ask another student to talk to them.", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "The paper cups needed for today's activity are not available.", "options": [{"text": "Cancel the activity.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Wait until someone brings them.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask the teams, \"What else can we use instead?\"", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Your team finalized the first idea they thought of to solve the problem", "options": [{"text": "Tell them to use that idea to save time.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask, \"Can we think of two more ideas before we choose one?", "correct": true}, {"text": "Give them your own idea", "correct": false}]}]}, {"index": 2, "title": "Student Leaders Toolkit", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Student Leaders have three important tools for successfully completing the program in their clusters.[[/H]]\nStudent Leaders have three important tools to help them in the program"}, {"type": "list", "items": ["Team Workbook", "MiniMakers Space", "People around You"]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Lets take a look at the team workbook.[[/H]]"}, {"type": "video", "key": "Common Module 3_With Subtitles_D4.mp4", "duration": 388}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Lets look at some actions you need to do during the program . Press the play icon to listen to the list.[[/H]]"}, {"type": "steps", "steps": [{"title": "Before Session", "text": "• Read the session completely\n• Confirm session timing and pen drive location with teacher\n• Inform your cluster to be present on the day of the session\n• Practise saying the long instructions out loud in your own style\n• Think about the last session, and remember who needs extra help\n• If anything is not clear, ask your teacher for help", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T08_55_07_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}, {"title": "During Session", "text": "• Go through pages in order - explain activities in your own words in Telugu, not word to word from the book.\n• Use the Answer guide to help your cluster. Most activities have many correct answers, not just one.\n• Remind your cluster about time, 1 minute before time is up.\n• If a word from last session comes up, ask students what it means. If they have forgotten, explain it briefly.\n• After each activity, tell teams what they did well. Use questions to help them improve - not corrections.\n• Stay calm and patient. If a fight is too big to handle, ask the teacher - do not ignore it", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T09_24_36_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}, {"title": "After Session", "text": "• Put every material and the workbook back in Minimakers space and make sure it is locked\n• Discuss with fellow SLs about the session and any problem you had. They might help you solve it\n• If any student was causing trouble, inform the teacher.\n• If you have any doubts, note them down somewhere in the workbook, you can ask the IIF team in your next training.", "audio": "ElevenLabs_2026-07-07T09_28_15_Anika - Sweet and Lively_pvc_sp100_s50_sb75_v3.mp3", "img": null}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "Practise Time: Choose the correct answer"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "If you have a doubt during a session, what should you check first?", "options": [{"text": "Mini Makerspace", "correct": false}, {"text": "Team Workbook", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "You see a Student Leader Say icon. What should you do?", "options": [{"text": "Skip it", "correct": false}, {"text": "Read and explain it", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "The video could not be played for some reason. What should you do next?", "options": [{"text": "Ask teacher to explain", "correct": false}, {"text": "Skip the activity", "correct": false}, {"text": "Use the pages in the workbook that explain the video", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "Before training, what is your homework?", "options": [{"text": "Do the activities at home", "correct": false}, {"text": "Read the team workbook and marks pages you have questions about", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "impact", "text": "The common module is complete. Congratulations!\nNow, continue to your level course for the next part of the course."}]}, {"index": 3, "title": "Problem Solving Process Part 1", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch this video[[/H]]\nPlay the Part 1 video of Session 2 to understand the details of the session and how to conduct the session with the students.\nసెషన్ 2 (S2) Part 1 వీడియోను చూసి, ఆ సెషన్‌లోని వివరాలు మరియు విద్యార్థులతో ఆ సెషన్‌ను ఎలా నిర్వహించాలో తెలుసుకోండి."}, {"type": "video", "key": "Level 3 S2 P1 - Training Prework.mp4", "duration": 499}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Practise Time[[/H]]\nAnswer the following questions after watching the video"}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "1. Systems Thinking is one step in the _______ skill, which is the focus of Session 2.\nసిస్టమ్స్ థింకింగ్ అనేది _______ skill కింద ఒక స్టెప్.", "options": [{"text": "Creativity Skill", "correct": false}, {"text": "Critical Thinking Skill", "correct": true}, {"text": "Compassion Skill", "correct": false}, {"text": "Grit Skill", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "2. In Activity 2, if a student is not able to write their superpower [strength], what should you do?Activity 2లో ఒక విద్యార్థి తన సూపర్‌పవర్ (బలం/ప్రత్యేక నైపుణ్యం) గురించి రాయలేకపోతే, మీరు ఏమి చేయాలి?", "options": [{"text": "Let them copy from others. Because the activity needs to finish on time", "correct": false}, {"text": "You write a superpower for them yourself in the book", "correct": false}, {"text": "Tell them everyone has special strengths and support them to write one together.", "correct": true}, {"text": "Skip that activity, and move on to the next activity.", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "3. Just like in Systems Thinking, the Problem Solving Process helps:\nసిస్టమ్స్ థింకింగ్‌లాగే, సమస్య పరిష్కార ప్రక్రియ మనకు ఏ విషయంలో సహాయపడుతుంది?", "options": [{"text": "Look at one part of the problem because fixing it can solve the whole problem.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Think about the solution and implement it quickly", "correct": false}, {"text": "Solve problems without checking if the solution creates a positive impact", "correct": false}, {"text": "Identify the different parts of a problem to understand how changes in one part can affect the whole system.", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "• A team understood a problem well and built a good solution, but they did not implement it properly. What will happen?ఒక బృందం సమస్యను బాగా అర్థం చేసుకుని మంచి పరిష్కారాన్ని రూపొందించింది. కానీ దాన్ని సరిగా అమలు చేయలేదు. అప్పుడు ఏమి జరుగుతుంది?", "options": [{"text": "The solution will not create a positive impact", "correct": true}, {"text": "The solution will definitely solve the problem.", "correct": false}, {"text": "The implementation step does not affect the other parts of the problem solving process.", "correct": false}, {"text": "The problem will disappear on its own.", "correct": false}]}]}, {"index": 4, "title": "Problem Solving Process Part 2", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Watch the Video[[/H]]\nPlay the Part 2 video of Session 2 to understand the details of the session and how to conduct the session with the students.\nసెషన్ 2 (S2) Part 2 వీడియోను చూసి, ఆ సెషన్‌లోని వివరాలు మరియు విద్యార్థులతో ఆ సెషన్‌ను ఎలా నిర్వహించాలో తెలుసుకోండి."}, {"type": "video", "key": "Level 3 S2 P2 Training Prework.mp4", "duration": null}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "5. What should you do when you see the Skip Video icon on a page? ఈ స్కిప్ icon ఉంటే మీరు ఏం చేయాలి?", "options": [{"text": "Always skip the page and move to the next one.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Skip the page only if the activity video has been played and everyone has understood it", "correct": true}, {"text": "Skip the page if the video has been played, even if some students did not understand it.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Never skip the page, even after playing the activity video.", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "6. What should students do in Activity 4 – Problem Solving Detectives? స్టూడెంట్స్ Activity 4 లో ఏం చేయాలి?", "options": [{"text": "Only circle the part of the Problem Solving Process that went wrong..", "correct": false}, {"text": "Only discuss what should be done to create a positive impact.", "correct": false}, {"text": "One team member should complete the activity while the others watch.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Discuss as a team to circle the part that went wrong and how they would create a positive impact", "correct": true}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "7. The Student Leader (SL) Guide has answers for Activity 4 – Problem Solving Detectives. As a Student Leader, what should you do?స్టూడెంట్ లీడర్ గైడ్ లో యాక్టివిటీ 4 యొక్క answers ఉన్నాయి. స్టూడెంట్ లీడర్ గా మీరు దానితో ఏం చేయాలి?", "options": [{"text": "Ask students to share why they chose that step, because there can be many ways to create a positive impact.", "correct": true}, {"text": "Read out the answers from the SL Guide before asking students to explain their answers.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Tell students there is only one correct answer and they must match the ones given SL Guide.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask students to circle the wrong step, without sharing the why", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "quiz", "q": "8. During the Problem Solving Detectives activity, only a few students are answering the questions. What should you do?\nProblem solving detectives యాక్టివిటీ చేసేటప్పుడు, కేవలం కొంత మంది స్టూడెంట్స్ మాత్రమే సమాధానం చెప్తున్నారు. ఆప్పుడు మీరు ఏం చేయాలి?", "options": [{"text": "Focus only on the students who are answering.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Ask Students to share and read different parts of the activity", "correct": true}, {"text": "Answer the remaining questions yourself to finish the activity quickly.", "correct": false}, {"text": "Skip the discussion and move to the next activity.", "correct": false}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "[[H]]Congratulations! You've completed the pre-work. You are ready to guide your clusters![[/H]]\nWhen we show up to the present moment with all of our senses, we invite the world to fill us with joy. The pains of the past are behind us. The future has yet to unfold. But the now is full of beauty simply waiting for our attention."}]}]};
